+The `Delegate` class is the engine's only data API. It listens for clicks and key presses on its
+root, the document unless you pass another, and routes each one by the selectors it resolves for
+each entity it serves. The `button` option carries the button's `classes` and `selectors` groups: a
+click inside a host the resolved `trigger` selector matches drives that host's button, and each
+button the delegate constructs receives the same groups. A replaced selector is not an alias, so the
+default selector then routes nothing. The driven engine is the one the static `find` method of the
+`Button` class returns, whoever constructed it, or an engine the delegate constructs and acquires
+when the host has none; an engine you constructed keeps its own groups. The button route prevents
+the click's default action, as Bootstrap's data API does. The `collapse` option carries the
+collapse's groups the same way, and § Components states its route under Collapse. The `dropdown`
+option carries the dropdown's groups, and § Components states its click and key routes under
+Dropdown. A click whose button host is one of the panels its collapse trigger names inside the root
+is refused when neither engine exists there, as § Components states under Collapse. A host under
+nested delegate roots is driven once per click for each entity whose selector matches, by the first
+live delegate whose root contains it to reach it. A listener that destroys a delegate during a click
+leaves every panel the click has not reached to the delegates still live.
 
